      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, often given as 850 mg three times daily. For extended-release it's 2,000 mg/day. This order is double the maximum, which raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nWas one of these intended?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day). This may be what was meant, since 1700 mg could be a typo or a mix-up with the 1,700 mg daily total.\n- **1700 mg/day split into two doses**, which is 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose.** Tell me the dose and frequency.\n\nIf you really want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first. Once you tell me the dose, I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
